From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eryk Wieliczko <eryk@wieliczko.ninja>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:19:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: apple: enable qualified J713 SuperSpeed host support

Add banked T8132 ATC calibration and the shared USB host startup needed
for the admitted J713 ATC1 port. Check inherited common-domain state
before taking ownership and preserve unsupported port profiles as USB2.
Keep display crossbar registers outside the mapped resources and support
the USB side of multifunction adapters without enabling DP output.

Publish the initial DWC3 host role before core initialization, propagate
PHY admission failures, and validate the Type-C SPMI response bounds.
Refuse suspend while a T8132 common epoch remains owned or incomplete.
Cover calibration bounds/order, failure unwind, inherited PMGR policy,
initial host-role ordering and transport lengths with host selftests.

The integrated driver has repeatedly enumerated a 5 Gbit/s SanDisk drive
through a multifunction adapter and completed matching read-only direct
512 MiB reads. Qualification is limited to ATC1; ATC0 stays USB2. Suspend,
10 Gbit/s operation and external display output remain unqualified.

Signed-off-by: Eryk Wieliczko <eryk@wieliczko.ninja>
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-6
(backported from commit 3949e3640d94d2b5434c84e9e1f6d7b81f650b70)
[j604: on j604/usb-idle-pm (omacom linux-aurora 1.607 + the T8132 idle
 runtime PM picks). Dropped: the PMGR apple,inherited-on contract
 (pmgr-pwrstate.c, its binding text and pmgr-inherited.py; the J604 keeps
 the ATCn_USB_AON parents on with apple,always-on, and ATCn_COMMON is
 managed, so nothing here needs it), the J713 board and policy hunks
 (t8132-j713*.dts*: this tree carries no J713 PMGR policy), and the
 original-loader adapter and m4-pmgr-policy harness hunks (files not in
 this tree). atc.c resolved to the Aurora integration form: the T8103
 dummy-pending check stays ahead of the T8132 dispatch, the legacy live
 PIPE lock retry stays next to the T8132 lock timeout, the USB3 phy ops
 get .exit next to the runtime PM wrappers, and atcphy_rpm_busy() gets
 back the common-power epoch term (and its KUnit case) that the
 1c79b03209 backport had to leave out. Host selftests:
 sn201202x-transport.py is taken in its Aurora integration form
 (f738b993b7, 8e656b0b69), which matches this tree's SN201202x driver;
 atc-t8132-usb3.py and dwc3-initial-role.py are not taken, as their
 source models no longer build against the later ATC and DWC3 code,
 in the Aurora integration tree as well (the KUnit suites cover
 these paths).]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
